"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[69293],{69293:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n<center>\\n<BookCard \\n          cover=\\"/assets/snippets/books/the-strange-house.png\\"\\n          title=\\"The Strange House\\"\\n          author=\\"Uketsu\\"\\n          publisher=\\"Readbe\\"\\n          publishedDate=\\"2022-10-27\\"\\n          isbn=\\"9791197708572\\"\\n          rating=2\\n          tags=\\"mystery\\"\\n        />\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nIt is said that a video titled <mark>Real Estate Mystery - The Strange House</mark> released on a personal YouTube channel gained popularity and was released as a book.  \\n<br>\\nIt is a composition that deduces the strange sense of incongruity hidden in a seemingly ordinary house floor plan in a dialogue format.  \\n<br>\\nIn a seemingly ordinary house floor plan, there exists a ```mysterious space``` that is completely isolated without being connected to any door.  \\nThis irrational structure felt a sense of incongruity, and the story begins when the narrator seeks advice from an acquaintance who is an architectural designer.  \\n<br>\\nThe way the story unfolded and the ideas were fresh. But that\'s about it.  \\nIt started well, but it was nothing more than forced motives, processes, and a patched-up ending.  \\n<br>\\nMaybe because I didn\'t know the video was the original, it was hard to read towards the end.  \\nIt wasn\'t because the content was difficult, but I was worried if I should continue reading this forcedness.  \\n<br>\\nShould something like this have been published? Such stories and developments definitely resonate more in videos.\\n"}')}}]);